\tag{fdip}
\title{Gauge fields, charges and sampling in lattice chirality}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{How does the index of the overlap operator of the
[Wilson kernel](fdip-0153) depend on the connection? When several species carry
charges, which condition on the charges keeps the coefficient functional fixed by a
cyclic rotation?}

\p{The first section concerns the Wilson operator with #{c_W=a/2}, any Hermitian
Clifford module with a spin grading, any nonzero finite-dimensional fiber and any unitary connection, unless a
statement names a restriction. The second concerns finite sums of species over a field with
#{2\ne0}.}
\transclude{fdip-0151}
\transclude{fdip-015A}
